<title>GREECE: Greek finmin says new interbank tax may be offset.</title>
<headline>Greek finmin says new interbank tax may be offset.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek Deputy Finance Minister George Drys told Reuters banks would be allowed to offset the new withholding tax on interbank deals against their corporate tax payments.  </p>
<p>The government will impose a withholding tax on interest on interbank deals made by banks operating in Greece, a finance ministry statement said.</p>
<p>The same statement said the government intended to tax the yields of new banking products effective January 1 in line with other European countries. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
